  "description": "Typed, checked LLM calls for .NET and C#. Extract structured data with OpenAI GPT or Anthropic Claude, read the reply as your own type and check it against your rules. Failed checks become findings for another attempt, within the attempt, model-call, output-token and time limits you set. Use calls on values, collections or [AIIntent] methods. A successful result means the configured checks passed, not that an answer is factually correct. Models come from an external provider file with openai and anthropic kinds. The core detects a changed target, document or provider file and runs your change handlers before the next target operation continues. Your application implements ITarget for its technology-specific operations. Add IntentSharp.Catalog for reloadable YAML or JSON intent files, IntentSharp.Guardrails for versioned rule files, and IntentSharp.Extensions.AI for a Microsoft.Extensions.AI IChatClient such as Ollama or Azure OpenAI, or intents exposed as agent tools. Commercial software, not open source: evaluate free for 30 days on development and test systems; after that, business use needs a paid license, and production use needs one from the first day (intentsharp.com/pricing).",
